# Generated pipeline outputs — ANCHORED to top level (2026-06-11, OQ-33 close session):
# the unanchored form silently swallowed ANY nested dir named outputs/, including audit
# evidence (KNOWN_STATE 2026-06-11). Never rely on this line to ignore a nested outputs dir.
/outputs/
# Chimera-era archived run outputs (332 files / 40M), never tracked — kept ignored by its
# own line when the anchor landed (status-quo preservation; track-or-not is an open call).
prolog/archives/datasets/original_json/outputs/

# Make stamps
.stamps/

# Generated Prolog artifacts
prolog/config_violations.log

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# OS artifacts
*:Zone.Identifier
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Secrets
.env

# AI tool artifacts
.gemini.snapshot

# PDFs: do not add new binaries to history (operator ruling 2026-06-13). Already-tracked
# PDFs under agent/analysis/originals/ are unaffected (gitignore does not untrack); this
# only stops NEW *.pdf (e.g. large source dumps) from entering the repo. Use `git add -f`
# to override for a PDF that genuinely must be versioned.
*.pdf

# CS migration backups and rollback remnants (generated by migrate_cs_facts_to_uid.py)
testsets_backup_*/
testsets_failed_*/
json_backup_*/
json_failed_*/
# `.claude/*` NOT `.claude/` — git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# `!.claude/settings.json` negation under a bare `.claude/` is silently inert (witnessed
# 2026-08-13: check-ignore still named the `.claude/` rule; the file reads as fixed and
# nothing changes). The trailing `/*` is load-bearing.
# settings.json is versioned project apparatus (the three hooks CLAUDE.md depends on);
# settings.local.json (personal permissions) and worktrees/ stay local.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Run-tagged pilot story dirs: intentionally untracked + glob-isolated + disposable (OQ-87).
# Canonical json/ stories live flat at json/*.json; other run-tagged subdirs (e.g. a live
# probe run) stay VISIBLE in git status until an operator rules track-or-discard.
json/pilot_*/

# Build artifacts — setuptools metadata regenerated by any `pip install -e .`
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
